# [audit] Steel-sector share of national gas reduced from 10 % (unsourced) to 3.5 %:
# India's gas-based DRI output FY2024-25 (8.88 Mt, MoS Annual Report 2025-26)
# x 0.21 t NG/t DRI (PNGRB 2024) = 1.86 Mt = 3.5 % of national gas (53.5 Mt).
# Pure-NG use is lower (PPAC FY26 sponge iron 0.98 %; MoS FY24 1.7 %) because part
# of the fleet runs on syngas/COG, which the NG-DRI route also represents. All
# values = previous x 0.35; the national-gas trajectory itself is unchanged.
# NG availability: BAU case (LoNG) slow national gas growth; steel-sector
# allocation only doubles (3.73 Mt by 2050 at a 3.5 % share; was 10.66 at 10 %) while steel demand grows 3.4x.
